WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.870
India sits in South Asia, between the
Arabian Sea and the Bay of Bengal,

2
00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:07.090
with the Himalayas to the north.

3
00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:11.770
In 2025, its population
reached 1.46 billion,

4
00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:14.910
more than China's 1.41 billion.

5
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.690
It holds about 87 per cent
of South Asia's people.

6
00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:22.630
Yet the World Bank classes
India as lower middle income.

7
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:26.590
So why is a country with more people
than any other still on that step?

8
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.950
Did it only recently open up to the world?

9
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.650
In this mission, you'll place
India in its region and the world,

10
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.730
and explore its context.

11
00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.790
Then you'll see how a federal government,

12
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:41.690
a young population and the
monsoon shape the country.

13
00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:46.760
Your mission: explain why India is still
only a lower-middle-income country.
